    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0554" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6176: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-21T21:00:00+02:00">October 21, 1940—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1001. Following information from excellent source believed correct: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Invasion of Greece is planned for early morning October 25. Duce has
                            given the order. Badoglio<anchor n="29" xml:id="d422-f1"/> strongly
                            opposed this move on ground that British Fleet will seize bases in
                            Greece from which to bomb oil fields in Rumania. Troops are being
                            embarked at Bari and Brindisi.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>It is reported that four large passenger steamers left Trieste October 18 for
                    Bari and Brindisi and it was inferred by Buffum<anchor n="30" xml:id="d422-f2"/>
                    that attack on Greece would begin in near future.</p>
                <pb facs="0555" n="543" xml:id="pg543"/>
                <p>Inform Navy Department that source of quoted information is Signor “X”.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="29" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>Marshal Pietro Badoglio, Chief of Staff of the Italian Armed Forces.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d422-f2" n="30" xml:id="d422-f2-content">
                <p>David H. Buffum, Consul at Trieste.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
